<title>USA: Video Update boosts authorized shares.</title>
<headline>Video Update boosts authorized shares.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Video Update Inc said stockholders Tuesday voted to increase the number of authorized Class A common shares to 60 million from 50 million at the company's annual meeting.</p>
<p>Video Update completed the sale of 6.1 million common shares in October, raising $25 million.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman said the approval of the authorized share increase was not a signal that the company plans to make another stock offer in the immediate future.</p>
<p>Video Update owns a chain of 243 video stores.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
